Parameters of Shared Information Learning Layer: the structure and parameters of this layer can be adjusted for specific problem. 
For spatio-temporal prediction tasks, we adopt the STGCN model with the following settings:
Number of nodes - 10,
Dropout probability - 0.1,
Spatial convolution kernel size - ks = 3,
Temporal convolution kernel size - kt = 3,
Batch size - 64,
Training epochs - 60,
Initial learning rate - 8e-4.

Parameters of Task-specific learning Layer: task-specific layers are constructed by stacking MLP blocks. 
Each MLP block consists of a fully connected layer, a batch normalization layer, and a ReLU activation function. 
The number of MLP blocks and the number of neurons in each layer can be adjusted. 
In our case study, we set the depth of the MLP blocks as 1.
